        "canonical_field": "essay:generated:question_68743848",
        "action": "fill",
        "value": "The gatherings I can speak to are ones tied to my own work rather than large industry conferences. I was selected as a national finalist in the Junior Science and Humanities Symposium for my Valley Fever research, where I presented an SIR-style epidemiological model I built in Python along with a microcontroller-based dust sensor I programmed in C/C++. More recently, ClarityAtlas, the iOS health product I lead technically through Open Health Intelligence, was selected for NSF I-Corps and the Johns Hopkins Pava Spark Accelerator, both of which involved cohort sessions, customer-discovery work, and demo presentations. Through that project I also presented to Johns Hopkins President Ron Daniels and leadership from the Johns Hopkins Data Science and AI Institute. I do not have a confirmed conference schedule for this year yet, so I would rather not list something I am not certain I will attend. On campus, Hopkins startup and Data Science and AI Institute events are where I spend most of my time, and those tend to draw students building real systems rather than only recruiting.",
